{
	"Name": "ScheduledSearch - Okta - System - Org - Possible Okta Denial of Service or Rate Limit Abuse [table]",
	"Description": "Counts Okta rate limit warnings and violations. Okta rate-limits per org, so sustained violations either mean an integration has gone into a retry loop or someone is deliberately burning the org's budget to degrade authentication for everyone.\n\nThreshold: 5 or more rate limit events in the window. Edit the eval near the end of the query to tune it.\n\nThis detection uses stats, so it renders as a table rather than shipping raw entries.\n\nReference(s):\n- https://developer.okta.com/docs/reference/rate-limits/\n- https://developer.okta.com/docs/reference/api/event-types/\n\nThis scheduled search is a dispatcher on \"Alert - Okta - Alert Router\". Its name is what appears as the alert name, so rename it here if you want the alerts named differently.\n\nIt ships disabled; enable it once you have reviewed the query and are happy with the volume it produces.",
	"Labels": [
		"okta"
	],
	"Schedule": "*/15 * * * *",
	"Duration": -900,
	"DefaultDeploymentRules": {
		"Disabled": true,
		"RunImmediately": false
	},
	"ScheduledType": "search",
	"GUID": "6d10016e-e1eb-5556-bde4-44d7b1033426",
	"SearchReference": "0f50782f-46a9-5e63-b2be-278afe52d6a6"
